<title>JAPAN: TOSHOKU TO FORGIVE Y49.4 BLN UNIT LOANS.</title>
<headline>TOSHOKU TO FORGIVE Y49.4 BLN UNIT LOANS.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japanese foodstuffs trader Toshoku Ltd said on Friday it would forgive 49.41 billion yen worth of loans to its wholly owned finance unit.  </p>
<p>The finance unit was struggling due to sluggish securities and property markets, Toshoku said in a statement.</p>
<p>Toshoku said that it had decided to forgive its loans to the unit as part of a restructuring of the unit's business.</p>
</text>
